Voxel Asset Registry public alpha

Software, Python generators, shaders, installation scripts and documentation:
MIT, see LICENSE.

The curated starter recipe data, palette, original demo geometry and demo
exports in the public release: CC0-1.0, see LICENSE-ASSETS.
Recipe data means registry YAML and entity _base.md files, including the
matching data in backend/seed/registry. Python and shader files in those
directories remain MIT.

The release manifest identifies the five starter families and their required
components. They are produced from project procedural recipes. The release
does not contain external character meshes, production body templates,
private reference images, manual Blender sources or personal iteration logs.
Dependency packages and the separately installed Blender/Godot applications
retain their own licenses; they are not relicensed by this project.

Your own imported references and created models retain the rights and license
you assign to them. The software license does not automatically apply CC0 to
your work. Optional ImageGen use requires a separately available image tool;
the local Impressor CLI prepares a request and does not provide that service.
